# MAYOR OF PRABUMULIH

# PROVINCE OF SOUTH SUMATRA REGIONAL REGULATION OF PRABUMULIH CITY NUMBER 3 OF 2021

WOMEN'S EMPOWERMENT AND CHILD PROTECTION

BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY

MAYOR OF PRABUMULIH.

Considering : a. that to guarantee Women's Empowerment and Child Protection in accordance with their dignity and to guarantee their right to life in accordance with their nature and disposition without discrimination and to receive Protection from Violence and other violations, legal certainty is necessary;

b. that to provide legal certainty in the implementation of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection as well as to carry out the mandatory affairs of the Regional government, regulation in the form of a Regional regulation is necessary;

c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, and letter b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation on Women's Empowerment and Child Protection;

In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic Number 3886);

3. Law Number 6 of 2001 concerning the Establishment of Prabumulih City (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2001 Number 86, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4113);

4. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as amended by Law Number 35 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning

Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 297, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5606);

5. Law Number 11 of 2012 concerning the Juvenile Criminal Justice System (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2012 Number 153, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5332);

6. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended several times, most recently by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);

7. Law Number 11 of 2020 concerning Job Creation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2020 Number 245, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6573);

8. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 1 of 2010 Concerning Minimum Service Standards in the Field of Integrated Services for Women and Children Victims of Violence (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2010 Number 56);

9. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 11 of 2011 Concerning Policy for the Development of Child-Friendly Regencies/Cities (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2012 Number 168);

10. Regulation of the Minister of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Number 4 of 2018 concerning Guidelines for the Establishment of Regional Technical Implementation Units for Women and Child Protection (State News of the Republic of Indonesia of 2018 Number 532).

# With Mutual Approval of THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF PRABUMULIH CITY and THE MAYOR OF PRABUMULIH DECIDE:

To Establish : REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING WOMEN'S EMPOWERMENT AND CHILD PROTECTION. CHAPTER I GENERAL PROVISIONS

