## Article 2

The implementation of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection is based on the principles of:

a. the best interests of women and Children;

b. gender justice and gender equality;

c. local wisdom;

d. law enforcement and legal certainty.

e. non-discrimination;

f. the right to life, survival, and development;

g. respect for the opinion of Children; and

h. law enforcement and legal certainty.

## Article 3

This Regional Regulation aims to:

a. guarantee the fulfillment of women's empowerment and child protection in the City;

b. serve as a guideline in planning, policy and strategy for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection;

c. protect and prevent women and Children from actions, decisions and policies that violate the rights of women and Children;

d. enhance the role and value of local wisdom as well as the role of customs in Women's Empowerment and Child Protection; and

e. serve as a legal umbrella for Regional Apparatus within the Prabumulih City Government that oversees women's empowerment and child protection in order to provide assistance and support to women and child victims starting from investigation at the police, prosecution to trial in court.

## Article 4

The scope of regulation of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection includes:

a. protection of women;

b. protection of Children;

c. fulfillment of Children's rights;

d. improvement of the quality of life of women and children;

e. community participation; and

f. guidance, supervision, assistance.

g. gender and child data system, disaggregated data on women and children;

## CHAPTER II

## IMPROVEMENT OF THE QUALITY OF LIFE OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN

## Part One

## General

## Article 5

(1) In order to improve the quality of life of women and children, the City Government is responsible for:

a. respecting and guaranteeing the rights of women and children without discrimination in accordance with human dignity;

b. enhancing Women's Empowerment and child protection in terms of role, quality and capacity in the fields of:

1. politics;

2. law;

3. social;

4. economy; and

5. culture.

c. strengthening and developing service provider institutions for Women's Empowerment and child protection in the City.

(2) The responsibility of the City Government in efforts to improve the quality of life of women as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by Regional Apparatus in accordance with their duties and functions.

## Part Two

## Implementation of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection

## Article 6

(1) The Mayor is responsible for the implementation of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection in the City.

(2) The responsibility of the Mayor as referred to in paragraph (1) may be delegated to the Deputy Mayor.

## Article 7

In implementing Women's Empowerment and Child Protection in the City, the Mayor designates the Regional Apparatus that oversees Women's Empowerment duties as the coordinator for the implementation of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection.

## Part Three  Establishment of Working Group  Women's Empowerment and Child Protection in the City

## Article 8

(1) In an effort to accelerate the institutionalization of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection in all Regional Apparatus, a working group for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection in the City is established.

(2) Members of the working group for Women's Empowerment and Child Protection are all heads/leaders of Regional Apparatus.

(3) The Mayor appoints the Head of the Regional Apparatus that oversees Women's Empowerment duties as Chair of the Working Group and Head of the Secretariat of the Regional Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Working Group.

(4) The establishment of the City Women's Empowerment and Child Protection working group is stipulated by Mayor's Decree.

## Article 9

The City Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Working Group as referred to in Article 8 has the duties of:

a. promoting and facilitating Women's Empowerment and Child Protection to each Regional Apparatus;

b. carrying out socialization and advocacy of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection to sub-district heads, Village Heads and Village Chiefs;

c. preparing work programs every year;

d. encouraging the realization of planning and budgeting that is Responsive to Women's Empowerment and Child Protection;

e. preparing the work plan of the Women's Empowerment and Child Protection working group every year;

f. being accountable to the Mayor through the Deputy Mayor;

g. formulating policy recommendations to the Mayor;

h. preparing a profile of Regional Women's Empowerment and Child Protection;

i. monitoring the implementation of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection in each agency;

j. establishing a technical team to conduct analysis of the Regional budget;

k. preparing a regional action plan for City Women's Empowerment and Child Protection; and

I. encouraging the implementation of selection and appointment of Focal Points in each Regional Apparatus.

## Article 10

(1) The Technical Team as referred to in Article 9 letter j consists of officials who understand gender responsive budget analysis as well as Women's Empowerment and Child Protection.

(2) The regional action plan for Regional Women's Empowerment and Child Protection as referred to in Article 9 letter k contains:

a. women's empowerment and child protection in laws and regulations in the City;

b. women's empowerment and child protection in the development cycle in the City;

c. institutional strengthening of women's empowerment and child protection in the City; and

d. strengthening community participation in the City.

## Article 11

(1) The Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Focal Point encourages the implementation of selection and appointment of Focal Points in each Regional Apparatus at each Regional Apparatus consisting of officials and/or staff who oversee planning and/or program duties.

(2) The Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Focal Point as referred to in paragraph (1), has the duties of:

a. promoting Women's Empowerment and Child Protection in the work unit;

b. facilitating the preparation of work plans and budgeting of Regional Apparatus that is responsive to Women's Empowerment and Child Protection;

c. carrying out training, socialization, advocacy of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection to all officials and staff within the Regional Apparatus;

d. reporting the implementation of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection to the leadership of the Regional Apparatus;

e. encouraging the implementation of analysis of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Budget; and

f. facilitating the preparation of Women's Empowerment and Child Protection data in each Regional Apparatus.

(3) The Women's Empowerment and Child Protection Focal Point as referred to in paragraph (1), is selected and appointed by the leadership of the Regional Apparatus.

# Part Four Improvement of the Role, Quality, and Capacity of Women in the Political Field

## Article 12

Efforts to improve the role, quality and capacity of women in the political field as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (1) letter b number 1 include:

a. carrying out socialization to increase women's political participation in general elections;

b. implementing programs that encourage the level of women's involvement in political processes and public positions;

c. facilitating women's self-development in organizing, associating and assembling; and

d. involving women in decision-making concerning women's interests.

## Part Five

## Improvement of the Role, Quality, and Capacity of Women in the Legal Field

## Article 13

Efforts to improve the role, quality and capacity of women in the legal field as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (1) letter b number 2 include:

a. conducting socialization to increase women's legal knowledge and awareness;

b. mapping and reviewing gender-biased policies; and

c. involving women's organizations in the process of drafting and discussing Regional legal products related to women's participation.

