## Part Six

## Enhancement of Women's Role, Quality, and Capability in the Social Sector

## Article 14

Efforts to enhance the role, quality and capability of women in the social sector include:

a. enhancement of knowledge and skills to encourage the fulfillment of education in accordance with existing potential;

b. enhancement and fulfillment of health quality for women;

c. enhancement of awareness and knowledge about independent, healthy and prosperous family planning including access to consultation services and marriage registration;

d. enhancement of women's awareness of the impact of early marriage;

e. facilitating and endeavoring the preservation of customs and the development of science, technology, arts and culture for the advancement of women;

f. conducting enhancement of women's awareness and knowledge regarding independent, healthy and prosperous family planning;

g. conducting programs to reduce maternal mortality rates; and

h. encouraging the establishment of women's organizations in the City.

## Part Seven Enhancement of Women's Role, Quality, and Capability in the Economic Sector

## Article 15

Efforts to enhance the role, quality and capability of women in the economic sector as referred to in Article 5 paragraph (1) letter b number 4 include:

a. implementing programs, activities, training to enhance women's skills and expertise in order to realize the improvement of women's welfare;

b. facilitation of business capital strengthening for women with weak economies;

c. marketing of products from businesses of women with weak economies; d. training for the development of women's capabilities through economic empowerment of pre-prosperous families; and

e. comprehensive entrepreneurship training for women.

## CHAPTER III PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN

## Part One General

## Article 16

(1) The City Government in its efforts to Protect women and children is responsible for:

a. establishing and implementing policies, programs and activities for the protection of women and children;

b. conducting prevention efforts against acts of Violence against women and children including criminal acts of trafficking in persons;

c. increasing the effectiveness of services for women and children victims of acts of Violence;

d. increasing protection efforts for female workers;

e. strengthening and developing institutions providing Protection services for women and children;

f. conducting cooperation with the Government, other Regional Governments, private parties, business sectors and/or NGOs in efforts to prevent acts of Violence against women and children; and

g. involving the active role of families, customary leaders, religious leaders, communities, and institutions in the field of Protection of women and children.

(2) The responsibility of the City Government in efforts to Protect women as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by Regional Apparatus in accordance with their duties and functions and may coordinate with relevant agencies.

## Part Two Prevention of Acts of Violence against Women and Children

## Article 17

In order to prevent acts of Violence against women and children, the City Government:

a. conducts socialization regarding the prevention of Violence against women and children by optimizing the role of customary institutions, Education, culture, religion and community organizations;

b. builds networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care for women and children victims of Violence;

c. provides public facilities that are comfortable and safe for women and children; and

d. establishes an Integrated Service Center for Women and Children Empowerment P2TP2A formed by decree of the Mayor and provides a Secretariat for the Integrated Service Center for Women and Children Empowerment.

## Part Three Effectiveness of Services for Women and Children Victims of Acts of Violence

## Part One General

## Article 18

(1) Protection of women and children victims of acts of Violence is implemented through integrated services.

(2) The provision of integrated services for women and children victims of acts of Violence as referred to in paragraph (1) uses the principles of:

a. gender responsive;

b. non-discrimination;

c. equal and respectful relationships;

d. maintaining confidentiality;

e. providing a sense of security and comfort;

f. respecting individual differences;

g. non-judgmental;

h. respecting the choices and decisions of victims;

i. sensitive to the background and condition of victims and the use of appropriate language understood by victims;

j. fast and simple;

k. empathy; and

l. fulfillment of women's and children's rights.

## Article 19

Forms of integrated services for women and children victims of acts of Violence include:

a. complaint handling;

b. health rehabilitation;

c. social rehabilitation;

d. victim assistance, enforcement and legal aid; and

e. repatriation and social reintegration.

## Part Two Complaint Handling

## Article 20

Integrated complaint handling services as referred to in Article 19 letter a are carried out by:

a. hospitals;

b. community health centers;

c. women and children service units;

d. trauma center shelters;

e. women crisis centres;

f. advisory boards for marriage guidance and preservation;

g. police;

h. prosecutor's office;

i. courts;

j. ministry of religious affairs; and/or

k. legal aid institutions.

## Article 21

(1) Complaints of acts of Violence against women and children may be made by reporters consisting of:

a. victims;

b. families;

c. communities; and/or

d. community organizations in the field of Protection of women and children.

(2) Reporters as referred to in paragraph (1) may file complaints:

a. directly;

b. by telephone; and/or

c. by letter.

(3) In addition to handling complaints submitted by reporters, the agency responsible for the Protection of Women and children, officers at service institutions as referred to in Article 20, are also authorized to conduct Assistance in handling victims of acts of Violence against women and children obtained through other information.

(4) Further provisions regarding the procedures for complaint handling services as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) are regulated by Mayor Regulation.

# Part Three Health Rehabilitation

## Article 22

(1) Health rehabilitation as referred to in Article 19 letter b constitutes efforts that include aspects of:

a. promotive;

b. preventive;

c. curative; and

d. rehabilitative.

(2) Health rehabilitation as referred to in paragraph (1) is conducted comprehensively, accessible 24 (twenty-four) hours, of quality and conducted in accordance with health service standards.

(3) Women and children victims of acts of Violence and children in conflict with the law have the right to free health services, including:

a. medical services;

b. medicolegal services;

c. psychosocial counseling; and

d. visum.

(4) Further provisions regarding the procedures for implementing health services as referred to in paragraph (3) are regulated by Mayor Regulation.

